{"name":"Interlude","hex":"#564355","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"interlude","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An intervening episode, etc.","An entertainment between the acts of a play."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To provide with an interlude.","To serve as an interlude."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interlude"}],"entries":[{"title":"Entr'acte","blocks":[{"text":"Entr'acte means 'between the acts'. It can mean a pause between two parts of a stage production, synonymous to an intermission, but it more often indicates a piece of music performed between acts of a theatrical production. But despite this, an entr'acte is often paired with a longer intermission, as an intermission is usually \"between acts.\" However, there can also be an entr'acte on its own, usually between the two acts without an intermission."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entr'acte","wikidata":"Q7114795"},{"title":"Interlude (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Interlude  is an anime and visual novel by Longshot told in parallel novel style that follows the events around three women. Interlude was originally released for the Sega Dreamcast on March 13, 2003, a rare occurrence for visual novels, as most are released for Windows first. PlayStation 2 and Windows ports were later also released. The PS2 version received a 'The Best' budget price re-release on March 1, 2007."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5b/InterludeDreamcastcoverart.jpg/330px-InterludeDreamcastcoverart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interlude_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q11287565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Alexandre_Lunois_-_Pendant_l%27entracte.jpg/500px-Alexandre_Lunois_-_Pendant_l%27entracte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik